         <component>
            <section>
               <id root="c9275027-bed9-2362-e053-2a95a90a657d"/>
               <code code="34068-7" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="DOSAGE &amp; ADMINISTRATION SECTION"/>
               <title>Directions</title>
               <text>
                  <list listType="unordered" styleCode="Disc">
                     <item>apply liberally and evenly 15 minutes before sun exposure and as needed</item>
                     <item>children under 6 months of age: Ask a doctor</item>
                     <item>
                        <content styleCode="bold">Sun Protection Measures.</content> Spending time in the sun increases your risk of skin cancer and early skin ageing. To decrease this risk, regularly use a sunscreen with a Broad Spectrum SPF value of 15 or higher and other sun protection measures including:
        
  
   <list listType="unordered" styleCode="Disc">
                           <item>limit time in the sun, especially from 10 a.m. - 2 p.m.</item>
                           <item>wear long-sleeved shirts, pants, hats, and sunglasses</item>
                           <item>reapply at least every 2 hours</item>
                           <item>use a water resistant sunscreen if swimming or sweating</item>
                        </list>
                     </item>
                  </list>
               </text>
               <effectiveTime value="20171204"/>
            </section>
         </component>
         <component>
